---
export const prerender = true;
import LegalLayout from "../components/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How the self-hosted Executor application handles data."
  lastUpdated="June 24, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Executor is open-source, self-hosted software. The active project does not
    provide an Executor-hosted cloud account, shared workspace, subscription,
    billing service, or desktop telemetry service.
  </p>

  <h2>Data stored by Executor</h2>
  <p>
    Your Executor server stores its application data in the data directory on
    the machine you operate. This may include the administrator account,
    sessions, hashed API tokens, source configuration, encrypted credentials,
    OAuth grants, tool policies, approval records, and request logs.
  </p>
  <p>
    The dashboard and API use this information to authenticate requests,
    connect the sources you configure, enforce tool policy, and show local
    operational history. Executor does not operate a central service that
    receives a copy of this data.
  </p>

  <h2>Connections you configure</h2>
  <p>
    Executor sends requests to MCP servers, OpenAPI endpoints, GraphQL
    endpoints, and OAuth providers only when required by sources and actions
    you configure. Those services receive the request information needed to
    perform the action and apply their own privacy policies. Review an
    upstream service before connecting credentials or invoking its tools.
  </p>

  <h2>Logs, backups, and access</h2>
  <p>
    The machine operator controls server access, log retention, backups,
    network exposure, and deletion of the Executor data directory. Anyone with
    administrator or filesystem access to that machine may be able to access
    application data. Protect the host, the master key, generated API tokens,
    and backups accordingly.
  </p>

  <h2>Website data</h2>
  <p>
    This repository does not define a shared analytics or account backend for
    the project website. A person or platform that hosts a copy of the site
    may process ordinary web-server information under its own policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Legacy products</h2>
  <p>
    Previous cloud and desktop implementations are retained only as archived
    source under <code>legacy/</code>. They are not active product offerings
    covered by this self-hosted privacy description.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about this project, open an issue in the
    <a href="https://github.com/davis7dotsh/executor-fork-testing/issues"
      >project repository</a
    >. For data handled by a particular deployment, contact that deployment's
    operator.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
